lean-hedgehog NEWS -- history of user-visible changes.

0.3.0 (unreleased)

  - withCoverFrom asks the minimums of cover only of a run of a number
    of tests or more.  A shorter run has only small cases, where a
    rare kind is rarer; every driver written for EthLib had made this
    by hand.
  - A report lists its classes in the order of their names, which is
    the same on every run.
  - Each report is flushed as it is printed.
  - Incompatible: check, apply and next of Command take the context
    first, then the command and the state, so a command that drives a
    system through a handle, or that may run at some forks only, need
    not carry what the scenario already has.  Each gains an argument:
    apply c s becomes apply _ c s, and so check and next.
    Command.wrap takes the context first too.  The line is two columns
    longer: where a structure literal went on below it, aligned under
    its first field, indent what follows as well, or Lean stops at the
    comma with "expected '}'".
  - Incompatible: StateMachine.applySut takes the model state before
    the transition as well as the one after it: applySut sut s t
    becomes applySut sut _ s t.
  - Incompatible: Config is PropertyConfig and Log is JournalEntry.
    Both short names met a Config and a Log of the code under test
    when a file opened Hedgehog beside it.  Code that sets a
    configuration with withTests and reads a journal by its
    constructors is unchanged.

0.2.1 (2026-11-19)

  - checkGroup takes a Selection: which properties to check, by parts
    of their names, and a size and seed to recheck in place of a run.
    Selection.fromEnv reads both from HEDGEHOG_ONLY and
    HEDGEHOG_RECHECK, so a driver replays a failure without a change.
  - checkGroup takes mustFail, for a group of findings: it is true
    when each property fails with a counterexample.
  - Property.lift takes a property to a monad that its own lifts to,
    so a pure one fits in a group of IO.
  - Gen.bytes generates a ByteArray, and bytesHex shows one for
    forAllWith.
  - A file that opens Hedgehog has BEq for Except, so === and tripping
    take the result of a decoder.
  - Gen.sample takes a size.
  - USAGE has a section of pitfalls, and says that a minimum of cover
    depends on the number of tests and that deterministic mode is for
    Command.fixed.

0.2.0 (2026-11-19)

  - Coverage: classify, cover, label and collect count the kinds of
    test case a property names, and the report lists each with its
    percentage.  A property whose tests pass fails when a kind stays
    below the minimum that cover asks for.
  - scenario takes a range of lengths for madhouse mode and a setup
    that runs before the first command.  scenarioFrom generates the
    start state, which no longer needs a default.
  - Command has buildIn, which generates a command for a state, and
    next, which says what state a command leads to.  Both have
    defaults, so an instance without them is unchanged.
  - USAGE says that Gen.sequence shrinks by removing elements.
  - Incompatible: Log has the constructor label, Status the constructor
    uncovered, and Report the field coverage.  A match on Log or
    Status needs the new case, and ⟨tests, discards, status⟩ a fourth
    component.  Command.gen and Command.fixed take the state after
    the context, and CommandWrapper has the field next; a list of
    them given to scenario is unchanged.
  - Not ported yet: the confidence of withConfidence and
    verifiedTermination, symbolic variables and parallel state machine
    testing, floating-point generators, diffs of the two sides of ===,
    test discovery.

0.1.0 (2026-11-18)

  - Generators with integrated shrinking: Gen, Range, Seed, Tree.
    Numbers, booleans, characters, strings, lists, arrays, options,
    choice, frequency, recursion, filtering, subsequences, shuffles.
  - Properties: property and propertyM, forAll, ===, /==, ensure,
    annotate, tripping, discard, evalIO.
  - A runner: check, recheck, checkGroup, and Property.report, which
    is a pure function for a pure property.
  - Hedgehog.StateMachine: model-based testing with transitions as one
    type, after proptest-state-machine.
  - Hedgehog.Command: model-based testing with commands as types and a
    MADHOUSE=1 mode, after madhouse-rs.
  - LawfulMonad Tree is a theorem.
  - Not ported yet: coverage (classify, cover, label), symbolic
    variables and parallel state machine testing, floating-point
    generators, diffs of the two sides of ===, test discovery.
